</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Method</span></h2>

<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04476v1/figures/cca_diagram.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/140;" width="333" height="140" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Diagram of the operations involved in the CCA block. This diagram describes the computation of the compressed latent query, key, and value vectors prior to performing standard Flash Attention on the compressed latents. The input <math id="S2.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is first down-projected using the <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{Q},\tilde{W}_{K},\tilde{W}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{Q},\tilde{W}_{K},\tilde{W}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices, then the two convolution operations are performed followed by the QK-mean operation, then normalization. For the V matrix, we do not apply any convolutions, but instead apply the v-shift operation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Preliminaries</span></h3>

<section id="S2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>1 </span>Multihead Attention (MHA)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Classical multi-head attention (MHA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2017</a>)</cite> operates on the input embedding <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}^{S\times E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}^{S\times E}</annotation></semantics></math> coming from the residual stream in a transformer, where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the sequence length and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is the residual stream dimension (we omit the batch dimension to keep notation clearer), and produces the query <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, key <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and value <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> matrices through separate linear projections of the embeddings:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=xW_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=xW_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=xW_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=xW_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=xW_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=xW_{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,k,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,k,v</annotation></semantics></math> projections are split into separate independent ‘heads’, such that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=[q_{1},q_{2}\dots q_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=[q_{1},q_{2}\dots q_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of heads. Each head has dimension <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=E/n_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=E/n_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. The intuition behind this is that each head can be operated on independently and in parallel by attention, allowing them to specialize in attending to different aspects of the input.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given the query, key, and value heads, we perform the softmax attention operation for each head independently then recombine the heads with the output projection <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{h}\text{softmax}\left(\frac{q_{h}k_{h}^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{h}\text{softmax}\left(\frac{q_{h}k_{h}^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.Ex5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">out</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{o}[o_{1},o_{2}\dots o_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{o}[o_{1},o_{2}\dots o_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is the head index. Due to the <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{h}k_{h}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{h}k_{h}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> term, attention computation scales quadratically in the sequence dimension. Since the <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q},W_{k},W_{v},W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q},W_{k},W_{v},W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices are of dimension <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\times E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\times E</annotation></semantics></math>, it also scales quadratically in the channel dimension. For autoregressive generation, we typically store each <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sequence element <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in the KV-cache, which is thus of size <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times S\times E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times S\times E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>2 </span>Grouped Query Attention (GQA)</h4>

<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S2.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:71.1pt;vertical-align:-34.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-175.6pt,36.2pt) scale(0.495521486816934,0.495521486816934) ;">
<table id="S2.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention</span></th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KV-cache</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.3.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward FLOPs</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.3.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decode FLOPs</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;">MHA</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4E^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4E^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2BSE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2BSE</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8BSE^{2}+4BES^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8BSE^{2}+4BES^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8BE^{2}+4BES" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8BE^{2}+4BES</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;">GQA</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2E^{2}+\!2\frac{E^{2}}{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2E^{2}+\!2\frac{E^{2}}{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\frac{BSE}{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\frac{BSE}{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\frac{1}{G})(4BSE^{2})+4BES^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\frac{1}{G})(4BSE^{2})+4BES^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\frac{1}{G})(4BE^{2})+4BES" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\frac{1}{G})(4BE^{2})+4BES</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;">MLA</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{2}+3\frac{E^{2}}{c_{kv}}+2\frac{E^{2}}{c_{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{2}+3\frac{E^{2}}{c_{kv}}+2\frac{E^{2}}{c_{q}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{BSE}{c_{kv}}+BSE_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{BSE}{c_{kv}}+BSE_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2BSE^{2}+4BS\frac{E^{2}}{c_{q}}+6BS\frac{E^{2}}{c_{kv}}+4BES^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2BSE^{2}+4BS\frac{E^{2}}{c_{q}}+6BS\frac{E^{2}}{c_{kv}}+4BES^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2BE^{2}+2BN_{h}{E^{2}})(\frac{1}{c_{kv}})+\frac{2BN_{h}{E^{2}}}{c_{q}c_{kv}}+\frac{2BE^{2}}{c_{q}}+\frac{4BESN_{h}}{c_{kv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2BE^{2}+2BN_{h}{E^{2}})(\frac{1}{c_{kv}})+\frac{2BN_{h}{E^{2}}}{c_{q}c_{kv}}+\frac{2BE^{2}}{c_{q}}+\frac{4BESN_{h}}{c_{kv}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;">CCA</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\frac{E^{2}}{C}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\frac{E^{2}}{C}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\frac{BSE}{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\frac{BSE}{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{2}{C})(4BSE^{2})+\frac{4BES^{2}}{C}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{2}{C})(4BSE^{2})+\frac{4BES^{2}}{C}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{2}{C})(4BE^{2})+\frac{4BES}{C}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{2}{C})(4BE^{2})+\frac{4BES}{C}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;">CCGQA</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\frac{E^{2}}{C_{1}}+2\frac{E^{2}}{C_{2}}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\frac{E^{2}}{C_{1}}+2\frac{E^{2}}{C_{2}}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\frac{BSE}{C_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\frac{BSE}{C_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\frac{1}{C_{2}})(4BSE^{2})+\frac{4BES^{2}}{C_{1}}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\frac{1}{C_{2}})(4BSE^{2})+\frac{4BES^{2}}{C_{1}}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\frac{1}{C_{2}})(4BE^{2})+\frac{4BES}{C_{1}}+\text{Conv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>Conv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\frac{1}{C_{2}})(4BE^{2})+\frac{4BES}{C_{1}}+\text{Conv}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
<tfoot class="ltx_tfoot">
<tr id="S2.T2.3.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 4.0pt;" colspan="5">
<span id="S2.T2.3.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="S2.T2.3.1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.T2.3.1.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> <span id="S2.T2.3.1.7.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conv term.</span> For CCA let <math id="S2.T2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}=E/C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}=E/C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.T2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of heads.
Conv‐layer parameters <math id="S2.T2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>ch</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Training FLOPs <math id="S2.T2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2BS\!\left(2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.551em;" width="0.551em"><mi>S</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>ch</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2BS\!\left(2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>;
decode FLOPs <math id="S2.T2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2B\!\left(2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.689em;" width="0.689em"><mi>B</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>ch</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2B\!\left(2\tilde{e}\,k_{\mathrm{seq}}+\dfrac{\tilde{e}^{2}}{h}\,k_{\mathrm{ch}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For CCGQA replace <math id="S2.T2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S2.T2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{e}=\dfrac{E}{C_{1}}+\dfrac{E}{C_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo mathsize="1.430em">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{e}=\dfrac{E}{C_{1}}+\dfrac{E}{C_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.T2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.T2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{q}+h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{q}+h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Kernel sizes are
<math id="S2.T2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\mathrm{seq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\mathrm{seq}}</annotation></semantics></math> (depth-wise causal) and <math id="S2.T2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\mathrm{ch}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>ch</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\mathrm{ch}}</annotation></semantics></math> (grouped).</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</tfoot>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE II</span>: </span><span id="S2.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of parameter count, KV-cache size, and computational complexity (FLOPs) for different attention mechanisms. <math id="S2.T2.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the residual embedding dimension, <math id="S2.T2.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the batch size, <math id="S2.T2.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the sequence length, <math id="S2.T2.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is the group size in GQA and <math id="S2.T2.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the compression factor in CCA. For MLA we use separate compression factors <math id="S2.T2.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.T2.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the low rank dimensions for query (with RoPE) and the shared KV-cache (we omit the shared key-RoPE and query-RoPE inference projection for the FLOPs calculation. This means that MLA’s FLOPs are actually slightly higher than shown). For CCGQA we introduce two separate compression factors, one for queries and one for keys and values, denoted by <math id="S2.T2.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.T2.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="S2.T2.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the RoPE dimension in MLA. We observe that CCA has both significantly fewer parameters and smaller KV-cache requirements than alternative methods and also, unlike all other methods, reduces the ultimate attention FLOPs required. A full table of notation can be found in Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table I ‣ I Introduction ‣ Compressed Convolutional Attention: Efficient Attention in a Compressed Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ainslie et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is a method that aims to reduce the KV-cache size by sharing the parameters across K and V heads. Specifically, GQA splits the heads up into groups and sets the parameters of all the heads in a group to be equal. For example, for two groups of four heads, GQA asserts the following equality: <math id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{g1}=k_{1}=k_{2}=k_{3}=k_{4};k_{g2}=k_{5}=k_{6}=k_{7}=k_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{g1}=k_{1}=k_{2}=k_{3}=k_{4};k_{g2}=k_{5}=k_{6}=k_{7}=k_{8}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since all the heads within a group share the same parameters, they do not need to be stored separately within the KV-cache, allowing us to achieve <math id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}/G</annotation></semantics></math> memory savings, where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of groups. MQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer, 2019</a>)</cite> is the extremal version of GQA with <math id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=1</annotation></semantics></math>, such that all pairs of key and value heads share the same parameters which reduces the KV-cache memory by a factor of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, this typically comes at a steep performance cost. GQA lets us interpolate between MHA and MQA to smoothly trade-off KV-cache size and model quality.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04476v1/figures/params_bar.png" id="S2.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/288;" width="476" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Parameter count comparison</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04476v1/figures/kv_bar_Slong.png" id="S2.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/288;" width="476" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">KV-cache at <math id="S2.F2.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=16384" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16384</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=16384</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04476v1/figures/fwd_line.png" id="S2.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/288;" width="476" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prefill FLOPs vs sequence length</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04476v1/figures/dec_line.png" id="S2.F2.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/288;" width="476" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Decode FLOPs vs sequence length</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Theoretical computational and memory complexity analysis across attention mechanisms with <math id="S2.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=2048</annotation></semantics></math>. (a) Parameter counts show compression methods reduce model size. (b) KV-cache memory at long context demonstrates substantial savings. (c) Prefill and (d) decode FLOPs exhibit quadratic and linear scaling with sequence length respectively. Note that these are theoretical FLOP counts. See empirical latency measurements in Figures <a href="#Sx4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ D.1 Benchmarking Setup and Kernel Notes ‣ Compressed Convolutional Attention: Efficient Attention in a Compressed Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>-<a href="#Sx4.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ D.1 Benchmarking Setup and Kernel Notes ‣ Compressed Convolutional Attention: Efficient Attention in a Compressed Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>. Our kernel implementation will be further improved through better operator fusion and memory access patterns. See Appendix <a href="#Sx2" title="B.1: MLA Inference Compute Considerations ‣ Compressed Convolutional Attention: Efficient Attention in a Compressed Latent Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">B.1: MLA Inference Compute Considerations</span></a> for more details on MLA inference considerations.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>3 </span>Multi-Latent Attention (MLA)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MLA takes a different approach to reducing KV-cache size. Instead of sharing parameters, MLA projects the K and V parameters into a smaller shared latent space <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{KV}\in\mathcal{R}^{S\times\tilde{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{KV}\in\mathcal{R}^{S\times\tilde{e}}</annotation></semantics></math> from which the full K and V can then be (lossily) reconstructed. Here, <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is the dimension of the compressed space. The compression is done with linear down-projections, such as <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{DKV}\in\mathcal{R}^{E\times\tilde{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{DKV}\in\mathcal{R}^{E\times\tilde{e}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x\tilde{W}_{DKV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x\tilde{W}_{DKV}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x\tilde{W}_{DQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x\tilde{W}_{DQ}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the KV-cache, we then only need to store the compressed representation <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math> which is <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}/E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}/E</annotation></semantics></math> times smaller than the uncompressed MHA KV-cache. In MLA we typically compress queries by a smaller factor than the keys and values. Given the compressed cache, the K and V heads are generated using separate up-projection matrices of shape <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}\times E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}\times E</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[q_{1},q_{2}\dots q_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[q_{1},q_{2}\dots q_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UQ}C_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UQ}C_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[k_{1},k_{2}\dots k_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[k_{1},k_{2}\dots k_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UK}C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UK}C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[v_{1},v_{2}\dots v_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[v_{1},v_{2}\dots v_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UV}C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{W}_{UV}C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the NoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> setting, MLA is advantageous as one can amortize all up-projections at test time and transform into MQA using the following relation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{softmax}(\underbrace{C_{Q}^{\top}{W}_{UQ}}_{q\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{h}}}\underbrace{{W}_{UK}^{\top}C_{kv}}_{k^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times N}})\underbrace{C_{kv}^{\top}{W}_{UV}}_{v\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{h}}}W^{o}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{softmax}(\underbrace{C_{Q}^{\top}{W}_{UQ}}_{q\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{h}}}\underbrace{{W}_{UK}^{\top}C_{kv}}_{k^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times N}})\underbrace{C_{kv}^{\top}{W}_{UV}}_{v\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{h}}}W^{o}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{softmax}(\underbrace{C_{Q}^{\top}{W}_{UQ}{W}_{UK}^{\top}}_{q^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times d}}\underbrace{C_{kv}}_{k^{\prime\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times N}})\underbrace{C_{kv}^{\top}}_{v^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}}{W}_{UV}W^{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{softmax}(\underbrace{C_{Q}^{\top}{W}_{UQ}{W}_{UK}^{\top}}_{q^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times d}}\underbrace{C_{kv}}_{k^{\prime\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times N}})\underbrace{C_{kv}^{\top}}_{v^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}}{W}_{UV}W^{o}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The case of RoPE, however, is more complicated. We cannot apply the RoPE rotation matrix directly to the <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math> cache if we want to merge up- and down-projections perfectly at inference time. In MLA, the key RoPE head is shared across all heads. To handle this, we define special RoPE heads and RoPE cache,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{RoPE}(W_{UQR}C_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{RoPE}(W_{UQR}C_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{RoPE}(W_{KR}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{RoPE}(W_{KR}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[q_{1},\dots q_{n_{h}},q^{r}_{1}\dots q^{r}_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[q_{1},\dots q_{n_{h}},q^{r}_{1}\dots q^{r}_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[k_{1},\dots k_{n_{h}},k^{r}\dots k^{r}_{n_{h}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[k_{1},\dots k_{n_{h}},k^{r}\dots k^{r}_{n_{h}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With the concatenated RoPE and non-RoPE query and key heads, attention is then performed as in MHA. By compressing K and V into the shared latent <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{KV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{KV}</annotation></semantics></math>, MLA can achieve significant reductions in KV-cache memory and attention parameters vs MHA. However, the up-projections add significant parameter overhead, and the shared key RoPE decreases expressivity of the positionally encoded information. In addition, since the q, k, v vectors are up-projected prior to attention, MLA uses approximately the same number of FLOPs in attention as MHA during training. During inference, MLA is advantageous due to the conversion of MHA to MQA via the amortized up-projections when memory-bandwidth bound (see Appendix B for a detailed discussion). While being parameter efficient, MQA is not entirely advantageous in multi-device inference in tensor-parallel settings, as each device would receive a copy of the shared KV latent before performing attention, which wastes potential expressivity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Compressed Convolutional Attention (CCA)</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed CCA method follows MLA and GQA in compressing the KV-cache, but performs attention purely in the compressed latent space. This enables RoPE to be seamlessly integrated without the need of special RoPE heads and projections, reduces the training parameter cost by more than <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> compared to MLA since we no longer require up-projection matrices, and reduces attention FLOPs by the compression factor <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E/\tilde{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E/\tilde{e}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be substantial even if it does not directly address the quadratic compute bottleneck. For instance, CCA with a <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="16\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times</annotation></semantics></math> compression enables <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqrt{16}=4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>16</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{16}=4\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer sequences to be processed for the same FLOP budget. Like MLA, CCA performs a linear down-projection of the queries, keys, and values into a compressed latent space. However, to maintain and enhance performance, CCA then performs three key innovations: convolutional mixing across both sequence and channel dimensions, q-k-mean, and value-shift prior to performing standard attention on the adjusted q, k, v.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first step of CCA is projecting q and k into the compressed latent space with matrices <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{Q},\tilde{W}_{K}\in\mathcal{R}^{E\times\tilde{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{Q},\tilde{W}_{K}\in\mathcal{R}^{E\times\tilde{e}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[\tilde{q_{1}},\tilde{q}_{2},\dots\tilde{q}_{n_{h}}]=\tilde{W}_{Q}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\tilde{q_{1}},\tilde{q}_{2},\dots\tilde{q}_{n_{h}}]=\tilde{W}_{Q}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[\tilde{k_{1}},\tilde{k}_{2},\dots\tilde{k}_{n_{h}}]=\tilde{W}_{K}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\tilde{k_{1}},\tilde{k}_{2},\dots\tilde{k}_{n_{h}}]=\tilde{W}_{K}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Unlike MLA, since we are performing the full attention in the compressed latent space, we compress the queries by the same factor as keys and values. In the CCGQA case, where we are repeating key and value heads, we can compress queries less, up to a multiple of the number of groups.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We find that performing convolutional mixing across both the sequence and channel dimensions (within a head) for q and k can substantially improve the resulting performance of CCA. Our intuition is that these convolutions give additional expressivity to the transforms learned in the latent space, and that this additional smoothing allows better information transfer and preservation through attention, similar to how the causal convolution prior to the SSM in Mamba <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu &amp; Dao, 2023</a>)</cite> improves sequence mixing performance. In a similar vein, recently-proposed “canon layers” are convolutional mixing layers applied across MLP and attention layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Allen-Zhu, 2025</a>)</cite>. Unlike canon layers, we only apply convolutions to q and k operations within the attention blocks, and use a sequence of two convolution layers instead of one. We find that mixing both across channels within a head (ch) and across the sequence (seq) is helpful.</p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{conv2}_{\text{seq+ch}}\big(\text{conv1}_{\text{seq}}(\tilde{q})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>conv2</mtext><mtext>seq+ch</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>conv1</mtext><mtext>seq</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{conv2}_{\text{seq+ch}}\big(\text{conv1}_{\text{seq}}(\tilde{q})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{conv2}_{\text{seq+ch}}\big(\text{conv1}_{\text{seq}}(\tilde{k})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>conv2</mtext><mtext>seq+ch</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>conv1</mtext><mtext>seq</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{conv2}_{\text{seq+ch}}\big(\text{conv1}_{\text{seq}}(\tilde{k})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
